


--> Fetch Types

    LAZY vs EAGER
    Fetch Type	Behavior
    LAZY	Loads data when needed
    EAGER	Loads immediately


--> Default Fetch Types
    | Relationship | Default |
    | ------------ | ------- |
    | OneToOne     | EAGER   |
    | ManyToOne    | EAGER   |
    | OneToMany    | LAZY    |
    | ManyToMany   | LAZY    |

--> Performance Impact
    EAGER → Performance issues
    LAZY → Better memory usage
    👉 Best Practice: Prefer LAZY

--> Cascade Types

    | Type    | Meaning        |
    | ------- | -------------- |
    | ALL     | All operations |
    | PERSIST | Save child     |
    | MERGE   | Update child   |
    | REMOVE  | Delete child   |

--> @OneToMany(cascade = CascadeType.ALL)
    private List<Employee> employees;



